exoplanet_mod.F90 is generated (ExoCAM 2.0).

  exoplanet_mod.F90.template   every planet/run parameter, documented, with the
                               aquaplanet defaults. Edit only to add or document
                               a parameter, never to set up a case.
  gen_exoplanet_mod.py         writes a case's exoplanet_mod.F90:
                                 template
                               + configs/<config>/user_nl_exo  (config defaults)
                               + $CASEROOT/user_nl_exo         (this case)

A case:
  1. install_sourcemods.sh <config> $CASEROOT/SourceMods generates the file
     (using $CASEROOT/user_nl_exo if it exists already).
  2. Set the planet in $CASEROOT/user_nl_exo: `name = value`, Fortran literals.
  3. Regenerate after every edit, then rebuild (the values are compiled in):
       gen_exoplanet_mod.py <config> --user-nl $CASEROOT/user_nl_exo \
           --out $CASEROOT/SourceMods/src.share/exoplanet_mod.F90
       ./$CASE.build
  gen_exoplanet_mod.py <config> --user-nl user_nl_exo --show  lists the
  resolved settings and the file each came from.

N2 is the fill gas and is always computed: exo_n2bar = 1 bar - (other gases),
or 0 when the others already exceed 1 bar, unless user_nl_exo sets exo_n2bar.
exo_pstd and the derived block (mixing ratios, molecular weight, heat
capacity) are computed by the compiler from the gas inventories and cannot be
set. Unknown names, wrong types and computed parameters are errors.

The values match exocam-casemgr's rendering exactly (same N2 rule, same number
format), so a case built either way compiles to the same parameters.
